iterranean Sea, its southern tip reaches the Red Sea, and to the east is Earth's lowest point near the Dead Sea. Jerusalem is the government seat and proclaimed capital, while Tel Aviv is Israel's largest urban area and economic centre.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"IL"},{"title":"Palestine","extract":"Palestine, officially the State of Palestine, is a country in the Southern Levant region of West Asia. It comprises the Israeli-occupied West Bank and Gaza Strip, collectively known as the occupied Palestinian territories. Israel has occupied the Palestinian territories since the 1967 war; the West Bank is currently divided into 165 Palestinian enclaves under partial civilian rule by the Palestinian Authority, and Israeli settlements under Israeli law in the West Bank settlements. Palestine share the vast majority of their borders with Israel, with the West Bank bordering Jordan to the east and the Gaza Strip bordering Egypt to the southwest. It has a total land area of 6,020 square kilometers (2,320 sq mi) while its population exceeds five million. Its proclaimed capital is Jerusalem, while Ramallah serves as its de facto administrative center. Gaza was its largest city prior to…","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palestine","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"PS"}],"arc":{"reports":166,"first_seen":"2026-10-10T11:08:52Z","first_title":"Israel election poll tracker: will Binyamin Netanyahu hold on to power?","first_url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMidEFVX3lxTE1ObDNEQkNJb0NDRHliRFh6ZGVlX2JvVkU3Q0FTSlFzVkNHM3FITER1SGFQdmlNNWZXQXpRNTYwM21CTDJmdFRQVWQtYXh4R2xLd0phaURJSC1RV210b1VCb2tnWlItM1dZMDc0NkRFQ1dudGd5?oc=5","first_publisher":"The Economist","earlier":[{"id":"e_ea71e6ce1b1b","title":"Germany takes cautious approach on Israeli election results","date":"2026-10-30T11:26:00Z","url":"https://www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79